.TH IP-AUDIT-CHECK 1 "November 2026" "Kea IP Audit Hook" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ip-audit-check \- validate audit logs and summarize per-file coverage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ip-audit-check
.I LOGS
[
.I LOGS
...]
[
.B --json
|
.B --table
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ip-audit-check
scans JSON Lines audit logs and reports record counts, event counts, time coverage, errors,
and reconstruction warnings for each file. It reads plain files and gzip-compressed files.
.PP
A base log path includes that file and numbered rotations, including gzip rotations (for
example,
.BR ip-audit.log.1.gz ).
Explicit files and quoted shell glob patterns are also accepted. The supported record schema
version is 1.0.0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Write the complete per-file summary and bounded diagnostic details as JSON.
.TP
.B --table
Write tab-separated file summaries and a separate diagnostics table.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I LOGS
One or more log files, base log paths, or quoted glob patterns. A base path includes that
file and numbered or gzip-compressed rotations.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Malformed JSON, non-object records, invalid event or expiry timestamps, unsupported schema
versions, and unreadable files are errors. Missing schema versions, reconstruction fields,
client identity, and invalid IP values are warnings. Missing fields are warnings because
intentional JSON field selection may omit fields without making a line corrupt.
.PP
The scanner continues after record-level errors. It reports up to 100 diagnostic details;
per-file and total counts include diagnostics omitted from the detail list. Time coverage
uses valid event timestamps only.
.SH OUTPUT
Readable text is the default. Each file summary includes records scanned, first and last
valid event timestamps, event counts, and error/warning counts. Table output contains one
summary table and one diagnostics table. JSON includes supported schema versions, totals,
per-file summaries, diagnostic details, and the number of omitted details.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scan has no errors. Warnings are allowed.
.TP
.B 1
One or more log errors were found.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or no input files could be resolved.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The command validates available records but cannot prove that events were lost unless logs
include sequence numbers or another completeness marker. Missing reconstruction fields may
be intentional custom field selection but can limit lease-history reconstruction.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
ip-audit-check /var/log/kea/ip-audit.log /var/log/kea/ip-audit6.log
ip-audit-check --json /var/log/kea/ip-audit.log > audit-check.json
ip-audit-check --table /var/log/kea/ip-audit.log
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip-audit-lookup (1),
.BR ip-audit-list (1),
.BR ip-audit-subscriber (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Kea IP Audit Hook contributors.
